      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.02-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Distance, area and gradient",
      "text": "Distance calculations at 1:50,000 use the linear relationship: one centimetre represents half a kilometre. A straight map length of four centimetres therefore represents two kilometres; six centimetres represents three kilometres. State the measured endpoints and convert to the requested unit. A result without a unit is incomplete, while a route length is different from a straight-line separation.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-1",
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-2",
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-01-1",
