      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.02-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The A–B–C–D training square has a two-kilometre side and area four square kilometres. On a true-size 1:50,000 print, each side is four centimetres and its map area sixteen square centimetres. The ratio between areas is the square of the linear ratio. The learner can check the result through either ground dimensions or appropriately converted map area; the two methods should agree.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-1",
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-2",
