    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.02-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Irregular areas can be estimated using a suitable grid. Count complete cells and combine partial cells under a clear approximation rule. A one-kilometre by one-kilometre grid cell is one square kilometre. Keep the estimate separate from an exact rectangle calculation. If the boundary is thick or the partial cells uncertain, report appropriate precision rather than inventing an exact surveyed area.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.2.02-1",
