    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.02-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A grid estimate can retain uncertainty. If a boundary contains three complete one-square-kilometre cells plus partial cells estimated to total one-and-a-half, the estimate is 4.5 square kilometres. That method does not claim every partial shape was measured exactly. A finer suitable grid can improve the approximation where the map resolution supports it, while a changed boundary would answer a different area question.",
