      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.02-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The direction of ascent can be stated separately. A at 1,500 metres and B at 1,540 means A→B rises forty, while B→A descends forty over the same separation. The gradient magnitude is the same, with the direction of height change reversed. Do not turn a descent into a negative distance or reverse the one-to-n ratio without stating the requested convention.",
